# Positive marketing / hire-page copy

When generating or editing **applicant-facing or marketing language** (WrapRider, WrapStar, JoyRider landings, heroes, band cards, emails, CTAs):

## Always positive

- Write what the role **is** and what the person **gets to do**.
- **Never** use “no this / no that / not like X” framing (e.g. “No middle handoff. No waiting on someone else.”).
- Prefer lines like: *Manage end-to-end, giftwrap items beautifully and deliver them yourself and brighten someone's special day!*

## First-visit / deep-link safe

- Assume the visitor **landed on this page alone** (e.g. clicked WrapRider directly) and knows **nothing** about other employee options.
- Do **not** assume they know what WrapStar, JoyRider, or other tracks are — and do **not** define this role by contrasting with those peers in hero/band copy.
- Optional peer comparisons belong only in an explicit FAQ or “compare roles” section the visitor chooses to open — never as the lead pitch.

## Tone checklist

- Positive verbs and outcomes (wrap, deliver, brighten, craft, carry joy).
- Self-contained: one track, one story, no prerequisite knowledge.
- Short, plain, exciting — not engineering rationale or process negatives.
